--   Test Description
--   
--   This test ensures that the GEM properly deals with excessive collisions in 10 or 100 mode.
--   
--   Functional Coverage
--   * Ensures that the GEM flags a collision frame statistic when more than 15 collisions occur in 10 or 100 mode.  
--   * Ensures that the GEM will not retransmit a frame when more than 15 collisions occur.
--   * Ensures that the GEM is able to transmit a frame after it is properly reconfigured.
--   
--   Detailed Test Description
--   
--   1. Initialise GEM for 10 or 100 mode operation.
--   2. Check reset state of loopback, half_duplex, and extint pins.
--   3. Enable all interrupts
--   4. Reduce back off time to one slot-time by writing bit 12 of the config register
--   5. write tx buffer q pointer
--   6. write tx_go (do not write tx_halt afterwards as we need to check that excessive collisions stops transmission)
--   7. Transmit a frame and at the beginning of the data portion of the frame cause a collision.
--   8. The GEM backs-off and one slot time later re-tries to retransmit the frame.
--   9. Repeat steps 7 and 8 fifteen more times.
--   10. After the 16th collision the frame should not be transmitted and a flag for excessive collisions should be set. Check that transmission is halted by too many retries.
--   11. Write tx_go bit
--   12. Check for successful transmission of a frame from the same tx buffer
--   13. Check status and statistics registers.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ten_meg_bit  -- 10Mbit/s operation (2.5Mhz tx_clk and rx_clk, 50MHz Pclk and Hclk)

-- ************************************************************************** --
--   1. Initialise GEM for 10 or 100 mode operation.
--   2. Check reset state of loopback, half_duplex, and extint pins.
--   3. Enable all interrupts
--   4. Reduce back off time to one slot-time by writing bit 12 of the config register
--   5. write tx buffer q pointer
--   6. write tx_go (do not write tx_halt afterwards as we need to check that excessive collisions stops transmission)
-- ************************************************************************** --

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 --  check reset state

apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbwr      04 00081000  -- reduce backoff time to one slot time
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd      14 00000000  -- read transmit status register
apbrd     138 00000000  -- check single collisions frames
apbrd     13C 00000000  -- check multiple collisions frames
apbwr      00 00000008  -- enable transmit
apbwr      1c ffffff00  -- write address of transmit buffer descriptor
apbrd      1c ffffff00  -- check transmit queue pointer
apbwr      00 00000208  -- write transmit start bit and enable tx


